# Who reviews what. GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a pull request changes,
# and the main branch's ruleset can require their approval. The last matching pattern wins.
#
# There is one maintainer for now, so the sensitive paths below name the same owner as the rest: they
# are listed so that a second reviewer (a person or a team) is added to them, and only to them, first.

# Everything.
*                                                       @iarsslen

# The cryptography, the vault and the formats other versions read: a change here can lock people out
# of vaults already on their phones. Byte for byte (CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md).
/mobile/lib/crypto/                                     @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/vault/                                      @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/export/                            @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/import/                            @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/backup/                            @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/recovery/                          @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/sync/                              @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/share/                             @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/sends/                             @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/keys/                              @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/pgp/                               @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/features/passkeys/                          @iarsslen
/mobile/lib/security_key/                               @iarsslen

# The fixtures other apps wrote, and the tools that copy the server's: never regenerated.
/mobile/test/fixtures/                                  @iarsslen
/mobile/tool/server/                                    @iarsslen

# Native code that handles secrets: AutoFill, the extensions, the manifests and entitlements.
